Depending on the purpose of the model, it is essential to distinguish
between best-fitting and best-predictive models. As was pointed out by Gu
et al (2001), the model class that can best accommodate a given set of anchor
points is not always the one that will make the best predictions on a high
anchor when having been fit only on some initial anchors. To understand the
learning curve of a learner on a given dataset, one is interested in a best-fitting
model class. For extrapolation, one is interested in a best-predictive one.Springer Nature 2021 L ATEX template
